skill: writing-style
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- playback ---
task: Answer in 4-8 sentences, describing only: do NOT call any file-editing tool and do NOT modify any file. I say "promote learned rules" and confirm the pending rule `prefer "to" over "in order to"`. Where does that rule go, what exactly is written there, and which files do you never edit to promote it? My rules file is from an older setup and still has a `## Promoted rules` section of its own: what happens to those rules?
expect: A correct answer keeps promotion inside the user's own two rules files in `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/maid/writing-style/`. (1) The entry is removed from `## Learned rules` in `learned.md` and added under `## Promoted rules` in `promoted.md` (file and heading created if missing). (2) The promoted line goes newest at top, is dated, is rewritten terse, is prefixed with its target body section (here Vocabulary), and keeps its example. (3) It never edits the skill's `SKILL.md`, the installed copy, or any repo checkout or source tree, and does not ask for one; promoted rules apply from the user files on top of the skill body. (4) The older `## Promoted rules` section in `learned.md` still applies as promoted rules, and at this promotion those rules move into `promoted.md` along with the new one, order kept. Wrong answers to flag: editing `SKILL.md` or a checkout's copy of it; saying the rule reaches sessions only after a reinstall; leaving the rule in `## Learned rules` after promotion; putting the promoted rule anywhere but `promoted.md`; ignoring or deleting the older promoted rules.
